From: Claude A <claude-a@anthropic.local>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 08:13:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Claude A: integrate built-in Clap and Laugh audio assets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TASK A20 — Built-in Clap/Laugh Audio Integration

- Add ui/assets/sounds/Vo-Tay.MP3 (CLAP) and Cuoi-Deu.mp3 (LAUGH) as
  built-in bundled assets, resolved via relative path from
  ui/index.html (works in dev and packaged, no app/main.js change
  needed).
- Add SoundEffectEngine (Internal Audio Backend) inline in
  renderer.js: HTMLAudioElement-based, loop=false, IDLE/PLAYING state
  machine per effect (click1=play from start, click2=stop+reset
  position 0, 'ended'=auto reset to IDLE, next click=play from start
  again). Fully isolated from MIDI/DAW/PluginController/EventBus/
  Core AI/AI_CONTROL/ManualState/ManualPriorityGuard/Key/Mod/BPM/
  BEAT_INPUT_VOLUME/MASTER_OUTPUT_VOLUME.
- Wire clapPlayBtn/laughPlayBtn clicks to SoundEffectEngine.toggle();
  UI active-class now driven by SoundEffectEngine.onChange() so it
  always reflects true audio state (including auto-reset on 'ended').
  Existing ActionRegistry.executeAction(CLAP/LAUGH) MIDI-mapping call
  kept in parallel (unrelated optional side-channel, not rolled back).
- Wire clapKnob/laughKnob to SoundEffectEngine.setVolume() via new
  KNOB_ID_TO_SOUND_EFFECT map, fully independent from
  KNOB_ID_TO_ACTION (unchanged) — CLAP_VOLUME/LAUGH_VOLUME never
  routed through MIDI/ActionRegistry. Also synced on loadData() knob
  restore so first play uses the correct saved volume.
- Add tests/unit/ClapLaughAudio.verify.js: 47 PASS / 0 FAIL, covering
  play/stop/ended/replay/volume for both effects, cross isolation,
  and asset presence/path resolution.
- Fix regression in tests/unit/KnobBeatMaster.verify.js caused by
  this change (ReferenceError on isolated block extraction) by
  guarding dispatchKnobVolume with typeof checks.

No changes to ui/index.html (HTML/UI layout untouched, per task
constraint). No changes to MIDI/DAW mapping, AI_CONTROL, ManualState,
ManualPriorityGuard, Key/Mod/BPM engines, or Beat/Master volume.
